---
// Demo — "Domains, Cloudflare & the registrar". A domain detail page (/domains/[id]) showing the
// two entity panels that together answer "is this domain actually pointing where we think it is":
// the Cloudflare panel's nameserver comparison ("Cloudflare verwacht" beside "Publieke DNS
// antwoordt") and the OXXA registrar panel, whose push box opens pre-filled with the pair
// Cloudflare expects. That composition is the point of the two modules.
//
// The story is deliberately *not* magic, because the product isn't: schakl pushes the delegation
// to the registrar, the registry publishes it in its own time, and the panel only changes its
// mind when somebody presses "Controleren bij Cloudflare" and it goes and looks. So the loop is
// push → wait → check → resolved, with a long, visibly empty wait in the middle. The panel
// reports drift; it never silently repairs it.
//
// Base frame = delegated, per the motion contract in showcase.css: with JavaScript off or reduced
// motion on this rests on the meaningful "after" state — public DNS answering with Cloudflare's
// pair, the panel's verdict reading that the nameservers point at Cloudflare, no attention list,
// and the registrar showing when the change was sent.
//
// Anything whose *text* changes is rendered as all its variants stacked in one grid cell and
// cross-faded with opacity (the DemoInvoice technique). `display` is never animated: it is a
// discrete property whose flip point across browsers is not something a marketing page should be
// betting on, and the failure mode is two nameservers drawn on top of each other.
//
// Strings: verbatim from messages/nl.json + messages/en.json wherever the app has them —
// cloudflare.panel.expected_nameservers / .observed_nameservers / .delegated / .not_delegated /
// .check, cloudflare.zone_status.pending / .active, cloudflare.issues.title, cloudflare.issue.
// nameservers_not_delegated, oxxa.panel.title / .expires / .pushed_at, oxxa.push.title / .submit /
// .success. The panel's verdict is one line of plain text and both of its sentences are here in
// full: the app has no delegation *chip* and no check timestamp (cloudflare.panel.checked_at is a
// key nothing renders), so neither is drawn here.
//
// Compression, stated the way the other demos state theirs: the client's name rides in the page
// subtitle. The real /domains/[id] header is the domain name plus an actions menu, and the client
// is the domains.company row of the Details card — a card this demo leaves out, because the two
// panels below are its whole subject. The status chip that used to sit in this header is gone for
// the same reason: in the app the status is a Details row, never a green badge beside the title.
import AppFrame from './AppFrame.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { sample, type Locale } from './labels.ts';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const nl = locale === 'nl';

// Cloudflare hands a zone a two-name pair like this; the previous host is a placeholder rather
// than a real company's real nameservers, which would be a claim this page can't check.
const CF_NS = ['bea.ns.cloudflare.com', 'cody.ns.cloudflare.com'];
const OLD_NS = ['ns1.hostingpartner.nl', 'ns2.hostingpartner.nl'];

const t = {
  domain: sample.clientWebsite,
  client: sample.clientName,
  // — Cloudflare panel
  cfTitle: 'Cloudflare',
  cfAccount: 'Atlas',
  cfCheck: nl ? 'Controleren bij Cloudflare' : 'Check at Cloudflare',
  zonePending: nl ? 'Wacht op nameservers' : 'Waiting for nameservers',
  zoneActive: nl ? 'Actief' : 'Active',
  expected: nl ? 'Cloudflare verwacht' : 'Cloudflare expects',
  observed: nl ? 'Publieke DNS antwoordt' : 'Public DNS answers',
  // The panel's verdict, both halves verbatim (cloudflare.panel.not_delegated / .delegated).
  notDelegated: nl
    ? 'Nameservers wijzen nog niet naar Cloudflare. Wijzig ze bij de registrar.'
    : 'Nameservers do not point at Cloudflare yet. Change them at the registrar.',
  delegated: nl
    ? 'Nameservers wijzen naar Cloudflare'
    : 'Nameservers point at Cloudflare',
  issuesTitle: nl ? 'Aandachtspunten' : 'Points of attention',
  issue1: nl
    ? 'Publieke DNS wijst nog ergens anders heen dan naar Cloudflare.'
    : 'Public DNS still points somewhere else than Cloudflare.',
  // — Registrar (OXXA) panel
  oxxaTitle: 'Registrar (OXXA)',
  expires: nl ? 'Verloopt 14-03-2027' : 'Expires 14-03-2027',
  pushTitle: nl ? 'Nameservers wijzigen bij OXXA' : 'Change nameservers at OXXA',
  send: nl ? 'Versturen naar OXXA' : 'Send to OXXA',
  sent: nl
    ? 'Nameservers gewijzigd bij OXXA. Het register publiceert ze meestal binnen een paar uur.'
    : 'Nameservers changed at OXXA. The registry usually publishes them within a few hours.',
  pushedAt: nl ? 'Verstuurd 6 aug 10:12' : 'Sent 6 Aug 10:12',
};
---

<AppFrame
  locale={locale}
  active="domains"
  nav={['dashboard', 'companies', 'contacts', 'projects', 'tasks', 'domains', 'invoices', 'subscriptions']}
  class="demo-dom"
>
  <!-- The domain's own name and the actions menu beside it, which is the whole header in the app. -->
  <div class="screen__head">
    <div>
      <div class="screen__title">{t.domain}</div>
      <div class="screen__sub">{t.client}</div>
    </div>
    <span class="muted dm-actions"><Icon name="dots" size={1} /></span>
  </div>

  <!-- Cloudflare panel: what the page stored, and what a check last found. -->
  <div class="card dm-card">
    <div class="dm-card__h">
      <span class="strong dm-panel">{t.cfTitle}</span>
      <span class="btn dm-btn dm-check">{t.cfCheck}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="dm-zone muted">
      <span>{t.domain} · {t.cfAccount} · </span>
      <span class="dm-swap dm-swap--inline">
        <span class="dm-zs-pending">{t.zonePending}</span>
        <span class="dm-zs-active">{t.zoneActive}</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <dl class="dm-dl">
      <div class="dm-fact">
        <dt>{t.expected}</dt>
        <dd>
          {CF_NS.map((ns) => <div>{ns}</div>)}
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="dm-fact">
        <dt>{t.observed}</dt>
        <!-- Both answers share one cell, so the column never reflows as the check changes its
             mind and the two labels stay on one line each. -->
        <dd class="dm-swap dm-swap--start">
          <div class="dm-ns-old">
            {OLD_NS.map((ns) => <div>{ns}</div>)}
          </div>
          <div class="dm-ns-new">
            {CF_NS.map((ns) => <div>{ns}</div>)}
          </div>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <!-- The verdict: one line of plain text under the comparison, which is how the panel states
         it. Colour marks the failing state only — amber while the delegation is wrong, muted once
         it is right. Both sentences share one cell, so the line never reflows. -->
    <div class="dm-swap dm-swap--block dm-verdict">
      <p class="dm-vd dm-vd--no">{t.notDelegated}</p>
      <p class="dm-vd dm-vd--yes">{t.delegated}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- The attention list exists only while something is actually wrong; it fades rather than
         unmounts, so the card keeps one height across the whole loop. -->
    <div class="dm-issues">
      <div class="dm-issues__h">{t.issuesTitle}</div>
      <ul>
        <li>{t.issue1}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Registrar panel: the box opens on the pair Cloudflare expects, which is the whole reason
       the two modules know about each other. -->
  <div class="card dm-card dm-oxxa">
    <div class="dm-card__h">
      <span class="strong dm-panel">{t.oxxaTitle}</span>
      <span class="muted dm-expires">{t.expires}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="field__label dm-push__h">{t.pushTitle}</div>
    <div class="dm-nsbox">
      {CF_NS.map((ns) => <div>{ns}</div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="dm-swap dm-swap--start dm-push__act">
      <span class="btn btn--brand dm-btn dm-send">{t.send}</span>
      <span class="dm-sent">{t.sent}</span>
      <span class="muted dm-pushed">{t.pushedAt}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="stagefade"></div>
</AppFrame>

<style is:global>
  /* Every beat occupies the same space (nothing unmounts, it only fades), so one height covers
     the whole loop. Measured in a browser on /features/integrations: the content is 31.3em at the
     672px stage, and the frame leaves ~2.6em under the registrar card. */
  .demo-dom .app { height: 35.8em; }
  /* Narrower than this the panel's own sentences wrap onto extra lines and the same content
     measures ~1.3em taller, which clipped the foot of the registrar card. Measured at container
     widths 33.7em / 36.7em / 38.5em (viewports 360 / 480 / 540) before and after. */
  @container (max-width: 44em) {
    .demo-dom .app { height: 37.3em; }
  }
  .demo-dom .screen { padding: 0.95em 1em; }
  .demo-dom .screen__head { margin-bottom: 0.7em; }

  /* One cell, every variant stacked in it, so nothing on the row moves when the state changes. */
  .demo-dom .dm-swap { display: grid; }
  .demo-dom .dm-swap > * { grid-area: 1 / 1; }
  .demo-dom .dm-swap--inline { display: inline-grid; justify-items: start; }
  .demo-dom .dm-swap--start { justify-items: start; }
  .demo-dom .dm-swap--block { align-items: stretch; }

  /* base = delegated: only the resolved variant is visible */
  .demo-dom .dm-zs-pending,
  .demo-dom .dm-ns-old,
  .demo-dom .dm-vd--no,
  .demo-dom .dm-issues,
  .demo-dom .dm-send,
  .demo-dom .dm-sent {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-zs-active,
  .demo-dom .dm-ns-new,
  .demo-dom .dm-vd--yes,
  .demo-dom .dm-pushed {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* The ActionsMenu trigger: the only control the real page header carries. */
  .demo-dom .dm-actions { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; margin-top: 0.15em; }

  .demo-dom .dm-card { padding: 0.75em 0.9em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-oxxa { margin-top: 0.65em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-card__h {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.6em;
    margin-bottom: 0.35em;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-panel { font-size: 0.95em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-btn { padding: 0.35em 0.7em; font-size: 0.82em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-expires { font-size: 0.8em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-zone { font-size: 0.8em; }

  /* The comparison the panel exists for. */
  .demo-dom .dm-dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.5em 0.9em;
    margin: 0.65em 0 0;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-fact { min-width: 0; }
  .demo-dom .dm-dl dt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35em;
    font-size: 0.75em;
    color: var(--mu);
    margin-bottom: 0.15em;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-dl dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    line-height: 1.45;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  /* The verdict line: `text-xs`, muted when delegated and amber when it is not — the app's own
     single colour decision on this panel. */
  .demo-dom .dm-verdict { margin-top: 0.5em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-vd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.78em;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-vd--yes { color: var(--mu); }
  .demo-dom .dm-vd--no { color: var(--amber-ink); }

  .demo-dom .dm-issues {
    margin-top: 0.6em;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 45%, transparent);
    background: var(--amber-bg);
    border-radius: 0.55em;
    padding: 0.45em 0.7em;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-issues__h {
    font-size: 0.75em;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--amber-ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.15em;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-issues ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    list-style: disc;
    font-size: 0.8em;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  /* The push box, pre-filled with what Cloudflare expects. */
  .demo-dom .dm-push__h { margin-top: 0.15em; }
  .demo-dom .dm-nsbox {
    border: 1px solid var(--bd);
    border-radius: 0.55em;
    background: var(--rz);
    padding: 0.35em 0.6em;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .demo-dom .dm-push__act { margin-top: 0.55em; min-height: 1.9em; align-items: center; }
  .demo-dom .dm-sent { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--done); line-height: 1.45; }
  .demo-dom .dm-pushed { font-size: 0.8em; }

  .demo-dom .stagefade {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--sf);
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 30;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    /* Playing, the demo starts from a domain that is not delegated yet and walks back to the
       resting frame: push at OXXA, wait for the registry, check at Cloudflare, resolved. */
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-zs-pending,
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-ns-old,
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-vd--no,
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-issues {
      animation: dm-before 11s infinite;
    }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-zs-active,
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-ns-new,
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-vd--yes {
      animation: dm-after 11s infinite;
    }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-send { animation: dm-send 11s infinite; }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-sent { animation: dm-waiting 11s infinite; }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-pushed { animation: dm-pushed 11s infinite; }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .dm-check { animation: dm-press 11s infinite; }
    .demo-dom.is-playing .stagefade { animation: dm-veil 11s infinite; }
  }

  /* Everything that is true only *before* public DNS has caught up. The two halves hand over
     rather than dissolve into each other: these are dense blocks of text in the same place, and
     a long crossfade of two paragraphs reads as a rendering bug, not as a transition. */
  @keyframes dm-before {
    0%, 55% { opacity: 1; }
    59%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
  }
  /* …and everything true only after the check found the new delegation. */
  @keyframes dm-after {
    0%, 59% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(0.25em); }
    65%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }
  /* "Versturen naar OXXA": present, pressed at 18%, then handed over to the result line. */
  @keyframes dm-send {
    0%, 15% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    18% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(0.95); }
    21% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    24%, 100% { opacity: 0; transform: none; }
  }
  /* The registrar accepted it; the registry still has to publish. */
  @keyframes dm-waiting {
    0%, 22% { opacity: 0; }
    27%, 40% { opacity: 1; }
    45%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
  }
  /* The registrar's own timestamp settles on the *push*, not on the Cloudflare check. The two
     panels keep separate clocks on purpose: from here until 59% the registrar half is finished
     while the Cloudflare half still reads "not delegated", which is exactly the state an agency
     sits in for hours — the push landed, the registry has not published yet. Sharing dm-after
     would have made the registrar look like it was waiting on a button pressed in another panel. */
  @keyframes dm-pushed {
    0%, 43% { opacity: 0; }
    48%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  }
  /* Nothing here updates itself: the panel changes its mind only when it is asked to go and look,
     so the press comes first and the answer follows it. */
  @keyframes dm-press {
    0%, 46% { transform: none; }
    49% { transform: scale(0.95); }
    52%, 100% { transform: none; }
  }
  @keyframes dm-veil {
    0%, 93% { opacity: 0; }
    97%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  }
</style>
